FMOV (vector, immediate), single-precision: implement the 2S/4S form.

Patch 0010 implemented only `FMOV_ASIMDIMM_D2_D`; `TryDecodeFMOV_ASIMDIMM_S_S`
stayed the generated `return false`. `fmov v1.2s, #1.0` is what a compiler emits
for `v2f x = {1.0f, 1.0f}`, and this killed a test guest before any of its checks
ran (TODO.md, verified 2026-08-11 and re-verified 2026-08-25 in patch 0010's own
diff context).

The operand shape is `MOVI_ASIMDIMM_L_SL`'s exactly -- arrangement specifier,
one written vector register, one 32-bit immediate -- so it reuses `MOVI_L_SL` as
its semantics and adds no new DEF_SEM. The only difference from MOVI is how the
immediate is built: `VFPExpandImmToFloat32` (already present, used by the scalar
FMOV forms) expands imm8 into an IEEE-754 single bit pattern where MOVI shifts
it.

